  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q79-84-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions, and express your answer as an exact value in simplest form.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q79",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1-\\cos60^\\circ}{\\sin60^\\circ}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1-\\cos60^\\circ}{\\sin60^\\circ}&=\\frac{1-\\frac12}{\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}}\\\\\\frac{1-\\cos60^\\circ}{\\sin60^\\circ}&=\\frac{\\frac12}{\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}}\\\\\\frac{1-\\cos60^\\circ}{\\sin60^\\circ}&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q80",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sec45^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}45^\\circ}{\\cot45^\\circ+\\tan45^\\circ}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "$\\sec45^\\circ=\\operatorname{cosec}45^\\circ=\\sqrt2$ and $\\cot45^\\circ=\\tan45^\\circ=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sec45^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}45^\\circ}{\\cot45^\\circ+\\tan45^\\circ}&=\\frac{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt2}{1+1}\\\\\\frac{\\sec45^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}45^\\circ}{\\cot45^\\circ+\\tan45^\\circ}&=\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{2}\\\\\\frac{\\sec45^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}45^\\circ}{\\cot45^\\circ+\\tan45^\\circ}&=\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q81",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sec^2 30^\\circ-\\tan^2 30^\\circ}{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac12$",
          "worked": "$\\sec30^\\circ=\\dfrac2{\\sqrt3}$, $\\tan30^\\circ=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt3}$ and $\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ=2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sec^2 30^\\circ-\\tan^2 30^\\circ}{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ}&=\\frac{\\left(\\frac2{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2}{2}\\\\\\frac{\\sec^2 30^\\circ-\\tan^2 30^\\circ}{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ}&=\\frac{\\frac43-\\frac13}{2}\\\\\\frac{\\sec^2 30^\\circ-\\tan^2 30^\\circ}{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ}&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q82",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ+\\cot30^\\circ}{\\sec30^\\circ+\\tan30^\\circ}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p5-q82-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{2\\sqrt3+3}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p5-q82-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitute the exact 30° ratios and simplify the compound fraction.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ=2$, $\\cot30^\\circ=\\sqrt3$, $\\sec30^\\circ=\\dfrac2{\\sqrt3}$ and $\\tan30^\\circ=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ+\\cot30^\\circ}{\\sec30^\\circ+\\tan30^\\circ}&=\\frac{2+\\sqrt3}{\\frac2{\\sqrt3}+\\frac1{\\sqrt3}}\\\\\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ+\\cot30^\\circ}{\\sec30^\\circ+\\tan30^\\circ}&=\\frac{2+\\sqrt3}{\\frac3{\\sqrt3}}\\\\\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ+\\cot30^\\circ}{\\sec30^\\circ+\\tan30^\\circ}&=\\frac{(2+\\sqrt3)\\sqrt3}{3}\\\\\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}30^\\circ+\\cot30^\\circ}{\\sec30^\\circ+\\tan30^\\circ}&=\\frac{2\\sqrt3+3}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q83",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$24\\sin^2 30^\\circ(1+\\sec^2 30^\\circ)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$14$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}24\\sin^2 30^\\circ(1+\\sec^2 30^\\circ)&=24\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2\\left[1+\\left(\\frac2{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2\\right]\\\\24\\sin^2 30^\\circ(1+\\sec^2 30^\\circ)&=6\\left(1+\\frac43\\right)\\\\24\\sin^2 30^\\circ(1+\\sec^2 30^\\circ)&=14\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q84",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\cot^2 120^\\circ+\\sec^2 120^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}^2 120^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p5-q84-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{17}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p5-q84-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the 60° reference angle and second-quadrant signs, then square the ratios.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In the second quadrant, $\\cot120^\\circ=-\\dfrac1{\\sqrt3}$, $\\sec120^\\circ=-2$ and $\\operatorname{cosec}120^\\circ=\\dfrac2{\\sqrt3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cot^2 120^\\circ+\\sec^2 120^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}^2 120^\\circ&=\\left(-\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2+(-2)^2+\\left(\\frac2{\\sqrt3}\\right)^2\\\\\\cot^2 120^\\circ+\\sec^2 120^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}^2 120^\\circ&=\\frac13+4+\\frac43\\\\\\cot^2 120^\\circ+\\sec^2 120^\\circ+\\operatorname{cosec}^2 120^\\circ&=\\frac{17}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
